
====================================================================================================
1. Symbolic checks (sympy), reconstruction gain g_c and true Luke gain g_t kept apart
====================================================================================================
(a) zero deficits: 1 - Y - (r g_t - g_c)(1-f)/(1 + r g_t) = 0
    at r = 1, no deficits: Y - 1 - (g_c - g_t)(1 - f)/(1 + g_t) = 0
(b) first-order expansion minus eq:19.5-first = 0
(c) 1 - Y - e minus the exact bound identity eq:19.5-bound = 0
(d) linear form (1+g_c)A - (Y + f g_c)B - r g_t (Y - f) at Y = Yexact: 0
(e) e(r) - [(1-Y) + (g_c - r g_t)(Y-f)/(1+g_c)] = 0
(f) calibration identity: Yexact - [(1+g_c)Y(0) + f(r' g_t - g_c)]/(1 + r' g_t) with Y(0) = A/B, r' = r/B: 0
(g) dn/dt = -n^2, n(0) = 1: Eq(n(t), 1/(t + 1)) ; dn/dt = -n^3/2: Eq(n(t), sqrt(-1/(-t - 1))) (time in units of t0)
(h) determinant (g_t,i = kappa g_c,i): kappa*(Y1*c1*c2 + Y1*c1 - Y2*c1*c2 - Y2*c2 - c1*f + c2*f) ; at Y1 = Y2 = Y: -kappa*(-Y + f)*(c1 - c2)
    equal ratios Y1 = Y2 = Y: Y(0) = Y ; r' = 1/kappa (= eps_eh/eps_cal)
    large-bias limit of the calibration identity: (Y_H + f*kappa*rp - f)/(kappa*rp)

